# The source file of this conversion, pinned.
#
# convert_bsi.py reads it from sources/ (git-ignored). The Validators
# workflow downloads it from the base below, checks it against this list
# with `sha256sum -c`, runs the converter and fails if the conversion in this
# folder comes out different. The bundle and the two coverage reports are
# therefore a reproducible record: a change of the kernel, of
# oscal_conv_lib.py or of the converter that would alter them is noticed.
#
# The base is the publisher's repository at commit
# 10f3c22898a4b15eb95fa228d78654cff32208e4 ("chore: publish rolling
# artifacts", 2026-10-30), which holds the catalogue version of 2026-10-29.
# The publisher rearranged the repository between the version of 2026-07-16
# (commit 39a1193f3d230828ea6614eb20c94a026c9f7df0, path
# Anwenderkataloge/Grundschutz++/Grundschutz++-catalog.json), from which this
# conversion was made until 2026-11-14, and this one: the catalogue a user
# works with is now the resolved catalogue of the control layer. The
# converter reads it under the name it has always read.
#
# base: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BSI-Bund/Stand-der-Technik-Bibliothek/10f3c22898a4b15eb95fa228d78654cff32208e4/
# into: sources
# path: control_layer/Grundschutz++/Grundschutz++-resolved_catalog.json -> Grundschutz++-catalog.json
#
592410c513691c18631402db3982dda6a4530dd6f2960868a6999017d311fa28  Grundschutz++-catalog.json
